<header><p class="enc-kicker">State</p><h1 class="enc-title">Kingdom of Lombardy–Venetia</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1815">1815</a>–<a href="/years/1866">1866</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/19th-century">19th century</a> · Also known as Lombardy–Venetia, Kingdom of Lombardy-Venetia</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Kingdom of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/lombardy">Lombardy</a>–<a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/venetia">Venetia</a> was a crown land of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/austrian-empire">Austrian Empire</a> created by the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/congress-of-vienna">Congress of Vienna</a> in 1815 from the former Duchy of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/milan">Milan</a> and Republic of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/venice">Venice</a>. Ruled from Milan and Venice under an Austrian <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/viceroy-of-india">viceroy</a>, it was a centre of Italian nationalist opposition and rose in revolt in 1848. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/austria">Austria</a> lost Lombardy to Piedmont-<a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sardinia">Sardinia</a> in 1859 and Venetia to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/italy">Italy</a> in 1866.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/kingdom-of-lombardy-venetia.jpg" alt="Kingdom of Lombardy–Venetia" width="320" height="213" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: FDRMRZUSA. · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Flag_of_the_Kingdom_of_Lombardy%E2%80%93Venetia_(1815%E2%80%931866).svg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
